    {
      "block_id": 12,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "The data types supported by the M68000 MPUs are bit data, integer data of 8, 16, and 32 \nbits, 32-bit addresses, and binary-coded-decimal data. Each data type is stored in \nmemory as shown in Figure 2-6. The numbers indicate the order of accessing the data \nfrom the processor. For the MC68008 with its 8-bit bus, the appearance of data in memory \nis identical to the all the M68000 MPUs. The organization of data in the memory of the \nMC68008 is shown in Figure 2-7. \n",
